      "content": "hey, i'm a middle school social studies teacher and i'm trying to put together a lesson plan about social movements and change. i want to help my students understand the different ways people approach these issues—specifically why some perspectives are seen as progressive and revolutionary, while others are seen as more regressive or stubborn. can u help me outline a lesson that explores these two sides?",
